{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1571831690,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTQwNzYwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545407606"},"message":"I think I like that approach. There's another aspect to it: At some point such a configuration might become useful to even record something that is not a URL one could actually git-clone from, but that could point to kind of \"special remote\" to retrieve a repo from by some different method.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1571851583,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTU1MDk3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545550974"},"message":"That sounds good to me too.\n\nThe proposed functionality could also eventually be used to create a command that rewrites `.url` values.  This would be nice in cases where `datalad create -d. \u003csubddataset\u003e` generated a useless URL and at some later point the subdataset was made available at a proper URL.  By rewriting the stored `.url` value, the clone would work outside of datalad.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1571864343,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTYzMzgyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545633822"},"message":"Sounds great.\nOne possible additional aspect: I think that it would be valuable if any such alternative record/source was accompanied by a name, which would be used as a name for the corresponding remote/sibling, as opposed to default \"origin\". with our current alterative locations we do try to reach its copy on its original location so origin as a name makes semantic sense to me. Also that one is most likely to contain desired commit/version. Alternative locations might not be that reliable, and we might need to try a few. For that it would be best to have them available in separate remotes.\n\nAlso, if there were names, we could finally implement support for other than /// shortcuts.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571901960,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTc4NDIwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545784207"},"message":"@yarikoptic I had a similar thought re names. However, I currently think that such functionality (configuring multiple remotes) would fit better into a URL rewriting command that @kyleam mentioned. Otherwise we would needlessly slow subdataset installation for plain one-off consumption cases.\n\nI will try to add the idea of named source candidate though, so we could have an easier time making the full feature set happen eventually.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571906884,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3Mzk4ODk4Mjk="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1571922725,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTkxMDg3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545910879"},"message":"\u003e Otherwise we would needlessly slow subdataset installation for plain one-off consumption cases.\n\nI want suggesting to add all known possible remotes, so I don't expect any effect on performance\n\nWhat I was thinking about is more of what should be instead of datalad.get.subdataset_url_candidate single variable, we might want to define sections similar to branches and remotes, and call them eg \"datalad.origin\" where each named section would have url field (for starters) but might later also define \"priority\" or cost fields so local configurations could be adjusted to reflect the situation etc","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571923782,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTkxODQwMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3827#issuecomment-545918403"},"message":"Hmm, I don't get it yet then. I cannot see a way to first guess possibly existing remotes (and it is guessing, because it is happening based on a superdataset's knowledge, but needs to be applied to a subdataset), and then end up with valid configuration for actually existing remotes without a cost. At the very minimum it needs a fetch for each remote. For each subdataset we already create two candidates (in the future more), each of them would need to be tested for each subdataset in question -- even in the one-off throw-away install case.\n\nI think we should decouple this from to ongoing PR.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1572278763,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Mjc0OTExNTcyMQ=="},"status":2}]}